battery-health-center (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix the Power Mode dropdown: choosing a mode was applied and then undone
    a moment later, because the page re-selected the old mode from a stale
    cache and treated that as a new choice. The cache is now updated as soon
    as a change succeeds, and dropdowns ignore selections that change nothing.

 -- Alexis Rios-Negron <182820807+arios4k@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:03:28 -0700

battery-health-center (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Release 0.3.0: new Power page with automatic power mode, GNOME power
    saving settings, power button and lid actions.
  * Package for Debian and Ubuntu: charge limits ask for a password through
    PolicyKit, and a systemd service re-applies a saved limit at boot and
    after sleep.

 -- Alexis Rios-Negron <182820807+arios4k@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:17:52 -0700
